{"task": "qft3", "run": 1, "round": 1, "temperature": 0.2, "llm_s": 64.93, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 412, "total_tokens": 10311, "completion_tokens": 9899, "prompt_tokens_details": null, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}}, "finish_reason": "stop", "reply": "**Step\u2011by\u2011step state evolution (global phase ignored)**  \n\n1. `|000\u27e9` \u2192 **X(0)** \u2192 `|100\u27e9`  \n2. `|100\u27e9` \u2192 **X(2)** \u2192 `|101\u27e9`  \n3. `|101\u27e9` \u2192 **H(0)** \u2192 `( |001\u27e9 \u2013 |101\u27e9 )/\u221a2`  \n4. **CRZ(\u03c0/2)** control\u202f=\u202f1, target\u202f=\u202f0 \u2192 unchanged (qubit\u202f1 =\u202f0)  \n5. **CRZ(\u03c0/4)** control\u202f=\u202f2, target\u202f=\u202f0 \u2192 `( e^{-i\u03c0/8}|001\u27e9 \u2013 e^{i\u03c0/8}|101\u27e9 )/\u221a2`  \n6. **H(1)** \u2192 `( e^{-i\u03c0/8}(|001\u27e9+|011\u27e9) \u2013 e^{i\u03c0/8}(|101\u27e9+|111\u27e9) )/2`  \n7. **CRZ(\u03c0/2)** control\u202f=\u202f2, target\u202f=\u202f1 \u2192 `( e^{-i3\u03c0/8}|001\u27e9 + e^{i\u03c0/8}|011\u27e9 \u2013 e^{-i\u03c0/8}|101\u27e9 \u2013 e^{i3\u03c0/8}|111\u27e9 )/2`  \n8. **H(2)** \u2192 `1/(2\u221a2)[ e^{-i3\u03c0/8}|000\u27e9 \u2013 e^{-i3\u03c0/8}|001\u27e9 + e^{i\u03c0/8}|010\u27e9 \u2013 e^{i\u03c0/8}|011\u27e9 \u2013 e^{-i\u03c0/8}|100\u27e9 + e^{-i\u03c0/8}|101\u27e9 \u2013 e^{i3\u03c0/8}|110\u27e9 + e^{i3\u03c0/8}|111\u27e9 ]`  \n9. **SWAP(0,2)** \u2192 ` (1/\u221a8) \u03a3_k e^{2\u03c0i\u00b75k/8} |k\u27e9` (up to a global phase), which is the desired QFT output.\n\n---\n\n```json\n{\n  \"n_qubits\": 3,\n  \"gates\": [\n    {\"name\": \"x\", \"qubits\": [0], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"x\", \"qubits\": [2], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"h\", \"qubits\": [0], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"crz\", \"qubits\": [1, 0], \"params\": [1.5707963267948966]},\n    {\"name\": \"crz\", \"qubits\": [2, 0], \"params\": [0.7853981633974483]},\n    {\"name\": \"h\", \"qubits\": [1], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"crz\", \"qubits\": [2, 1], \"params\": [1.5707963267948966]},\n    {\"name\": \"h\", \"qubits\": [2], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"swap\", \"qubits\": [0, 2], \"params\": []}\n  ],\n  \"note\": \"QFT on |101> yields the desired state up to a global phase\"\n}\n```", "reasoning_chars": 24115, "spec": {"n_qubits": 3, "gates": [{"name": "x", "qubits": [0], "params": []}, {"name": "x", "qubits": [2], "params": []}, {"name": "h", "qubits": [0], "params": []}, {"name": "crz", "qubits": [1, 0], "params": [1.5707963267948966]}, {"name": "crz", "qubits": [2, 0], "params": [0.7853981633974483]}, {"name": "h", "qubits": [1], "params": []}, {"name": "crz", "qubits": [2, 1], "params": [1.5707963267948966]}, {"name": "h", "qubits": [2], "params": []}, {"name": "swap", "qubits": [0, 2], "params": []}], "note": "QFT on |101> yields the desired state up to a global phase"}, "notes": [], "logical_2q": 4, "fidelity_logical": 0.9999999999999991, "compile_s": 0.1669, "routed_2q": 12, "routed_swaps": 0, "depth": 29, "q3_s": 0.0556, "q3_2q": 9, "fidelity_compiled": 0.9999999999999993, "leak": 3.3306690738754696e-16, "largest_component": 3, "sim_s": 0.1195, "feedback": "Result of your circuit: fidelity with the target state = 1.000000 (before compiling); after compiling for the device: fidelity = 1.000000, two-qubit gates on the device = 12 (you used 4), depth = 29. The state is correct. If you can, give a circuit with fewer two-qubit gates on the device that is still exact; otherwise repeat your circuit."}
{"task": "qft3", "run": 1, "round": 2, "temperature": 0.2, "llm_s": 60.938, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 1243, "total_tokens": 13057, "completion_tokens": 11814, "prompt_tokens_details": null, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}}, "finish_reason": "stop", "reply": "**Explanation**\n\nBecause the input state\u202f|101\u27e9 is known, every controlled\u2011phase gate in the 3\u2011qubit QFT can be replaced by a single\u2011qubit\u202fRz rotation on the target (the control qubit is\u202f1).  \nThe final SWAP that normally restores the bit order is unnecessary if we run the QFT in reversed qubit order (apply the operations on qubit\u202f2, then\u202f1, then\u202f0).  \nThus the whole transform is realized with only single\u2011qubit gates (X, H, Rz), i.e. **zero two\u2011qubit gates**.\n\n---\n\n```json\n{\n  \"n_qubits\": 3,\n  \"gates\": [\n    {\"name\": \"x\",  \"qubits\": [0], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"x\",  \"qubits\": [2], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"h\",  \"qubits\": [2], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"rz\", \"qubits\": [2], \"params\": [0.7853981633974483]},   // \u03c0/4\n    {\"name\": \"h\",  \"qubits\": [1], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"rz\", \"qubits\": [1], \"params\": [1.5707963267948966]},   // \u03c0/2\n    {\"name\": \"h\",  \"qubits\": [0], \"params\": []}\n  ],\n  \"note\": \"Exact QFT on |101> using only single\u2011qubit gates (no two\u2011qubit gates).\"\n}\n```", "reasoning_chars": 33752, "spec": {"n_qubits": 3, "gates": [{"name": "x", "qubits": [0], "params": []}, {"name": "x", "qubits": [2], "params": []}, {"name": "h", "qubits": [2], "params": []}, {"name": "rz", "qubits": [2], "params": [0.7853981633974483]}, {"name": "h", "qubits": [1], "params": []}, {"name": "rz", "qubits": [1], "params": [1.5707963267948966]}, {"name": "h", "qubits": [0], "params": []}], "note": "Exact QFT on |101> using only single\u2011qubit gates (no two\u2011qubit gates)."}, "notes": [], "logical_2q": 0, "fidelity_logical": 0.