{"task": "qft3", "run": 1, "round": 3, "temperature": 0.2, "llm_s": 60.09, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 1688, "total_tokens": 13159, "completion_tokens": 11471, "prompt_tokens_details": null, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}}, "finish_reason": "stop", "reply": "**Step\u2011by\u2011step (brief)**  \n\n1.\u202f|000\u27e9 \u2192 **X\u202f0** \u2192 |100\u27e9  \n2.\u202f|100\u27e9 \u2192 **X\u202f2** \u2192 |101\u27e9  \n3.\u202f|101\u27e9 \u2192 **H\u202f2** \u2192 (|100\u27e9\u202f\u2212\u202f|101\u27e9)/\u221a2  \n4.\u202f\u2192 **Rz\u202f2(\u03c0/4)** \u2192 (e^{-i\u03c0/8}|100\u27e9\u202f\u2212\u202fe^{i\u03c0/8}|101\u27e9)/\u221a2  \n5.\u202f\u2192 **H\u202f1** \u2192 (1/2)[ e^{-i\u03c0/8}(|100\u27e9+|110\u27e9)\u202f\u2212\u202fe^{i\u03c0/8}(|101\u27e9+|111\u27e9) ]  \n6.\u202f\u2192 **Rz\u202f1(\u03c0/2)** \u2192 (1/2)[ e^{-i3\u03c0/8}|100\u27e9\u202f+\u202fe^{i\u03c0/8}|110\u27e9\u202f\u2212\u202fe^{-i\u03c0/8}|101\u27e9\u202f\u2212\u202fe^{i3\u03c0/8}|111\u27e9 ]  \n7.\u202f\u2192 **H\u202f0** \u2192 (1/(2\u221a2))[ e^{-i3\u03c0/8}|000\u27e9\u202f\u2212\u202fe^{-i3\u03c0/8}|100\u27e9\u202f+\u202fe^{i\u03c0/8}|010\u27e9\u202f\u2212\u202fe^{i\u03c0/8}|110\u27e9\u202f\u2212\u202fe^{-i\u03c0/8}|001\u27e9\u202f+\u202fe^{-i\u03c0/8}|101\u27e9\u202f\u2212\u202fe^{i3\u03c0/8}|011\u27e9\u202f+\u202fe^{i3\u03c0/8}|111\u27e9 ]  \n\nThe overall state equals a global phase\u202fe^{-i3\u03c0/8}\u202ftimes  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\sum_{k=0}^{7} e^{2\\pi i\\,5k/8}\\,|k\\rangle,\n\\]  \n\nwhich is exactly the desired 3\u2011qubit QFT of |101\u27e9.\n\n---\n\n```json\n{\n  \"n_qubits\": 3,\n  \"gates\": [\n    {\"name\": \"x\",  \"qubits\": [0], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"x\",  \"qubits\": [2], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"h\",  \"qubits\": [2], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"rz\", \"qubits\": [2], \"params\": [0.7853981633974483]},   // \u03c0/4\n    {\"name\": \"h\",  \"qubits\": [1], \"params\": []},\n    {\"name\": \"rz\", \"qubits\": [1], \"params\": [1.5707963267948966]},   // \u03c0/2\n    {\"name\": \"h\",  \"qubits\": [0], \"params\": []}\n  ],\n  \"note\": \"Exact QFT on |101> using only single\u2011qubit gates (no two\u2011qubit gates).\"\n}\n```", "reasoning_chars": 27942, "spec": {"n_qubits": 3, "gates": [{"name": "x", "qubits": [0], "params": []}, {"name": "x", "qubits": [2], "params": []}, {"name": "h", "qubits": [2], "params": []}, {"name": "rz", "qubits": [2], "params": [0.7853981633974483]}, {"name": "h", "qubits": [1], "params": []}, {"name": "rz", "qubits": [1], "params": [1.5707963267948966]}, {"name": "h", "qubits": [0], "params": []}], "note": "Exact QFT on |101> using only single\u2011qubit gates (no two\u2011qubit gates)."}, "notes": [], "logical_2q": 0, "fidelity_logical": 0.9999999999999991, "compile_s": 0.0232, "routed_2q": 0, "routed_swaps": 0, "depth": 3, "q3_s": 0.0174, "q3_2q": 0, "fidelity_compiled": 0.9999999999999996, "leak": 1.1102230246251565e-16, "largest_component": 3, "sim_s": 0.0068, "feedback": "Result of your circuit: fidelity with the target state = 1.000000 (before compiling); after compiling for the device: fidelity = 1.000000, two-qubit gates on the device = 0 (you used 0), depth = 3. The state is correct. If you can, give a circuit with fewer two-qubit gates on the device that is still exact; otherwise repeat your circuit."}
